{title: He Changed Me}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

>Lyrics

Once on a road to nowhere,

Now I am headed somewhere;

Life is a brand-new game,

Since He changed me!

Jesus my Lord and Savior

Here in my heart forever;

Born from above, I know

That He changed me!

Gone are the fears that kept me enslaved.

Brought into the light of day, I'm saved.

Transformed by a revelation,

I am a new creation,

No longer a slave to sin,

For He changed me!

Piano Solo

God in His Word reminds us,

It is our sin that binds us;

Only His power and love

Could have changed me.

Exchanging my chains for freedom,

Now I am in His kingdom;

I am a child of God,

For He changed me!

Gone are the fears that kept me enslaved.

Brought into the light of day, I'm saved.

Transformed by a revelation,

I am a new creation,

No longer a slave to sin,

For He changed me, changed me,

Changed me... I'm free!
